Cell["\<\
The separation stays below half the graph radius. Near the boundary the \
available ball centres cannot cut away enough vertices, so even the hull of a \
pair fattens. These finite-window exponents need room around the points.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5dce8d9c-80dc-498f-9ae7-1188c677a704"],

Cell["A radius bound gives a lens", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c264cfab-df02-4248-a4fe-bd8ca63b7a12"],

Cell["\<\
A bound admits only enclosing balls with radius at most that bound. \
Increasing it admits more balls, so their intersection shrinks.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ea8538bd-bc15-4fb6-ba74-bf070a59528e"],

Cell["\<\
Below the least enclosing radius there is no such ball; the empty \
intersection is the whole graph.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fe4ff2dc-b957-421a-8e18-5d8d77e724d6"],

Cell["\<\
Starting at the least enclosing radius, the lens thins towards the \
unrestricted ball hull. On a finite mesh the final hull can retain a few \
vertices across its width.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"592f904a-a02f-48b1-a878-fa8c318a0797"],

Cell["\<\
The same pair is shown under increasing radius bounds, followed by its \
unrestricted hull. The table also checks that each hull is contained in the \
preceding one.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4dcd072e-bdb7-4a3f-a20e-f8004ce1ccfc"],

